WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.210
In northern India, at about thirty-five,
the Buddha reaches awakening.

2
00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:07.840
Around the age of eighty, he dies.

3
00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:10.750
Buddhists call both moments nibbana.

4
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.240
The word means blowing
out, as a flame goes out.

5
00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:16.920
Yet many Buddhists say
it is unconditioned,

6
00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:19.090
and cannot be fully explained.

7
00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:24.030
So if the Buddhist goal is beyond
words, how can anyone aim for it?

8
00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:27.180
In this mission, you'll
see nibbana in this life,

9
00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:29.140
and what changes at death.

10
00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:33.780
Then you'll compare how Theravada and
Mahayana Buddhists picture the goal.

11
00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:39.160
Your mission: find out how Buddhists can
aim for a goal that words cannot capture.
